      "severity": "minor",
      "supported_identity_reconciliation": true,
      "reason": "Both full primary tables establish the identical thirteen solutes and their literal masses, one litre distilled-water input, and unquantified NaOH used after NTA dissolution to pH6.5. Final pH7.0 is a stated resulting condition. V2 correctly reconciles nominal formulation identity and scopes but its active notes infer a possible further adjustment/addition to justify UNKNOWN membership. The source does not instruct a second titration. Unknown quantity does not decide constituent-list completeness under ComponentCompletenessEnum.",
      "required_change": "Use COMPLETE relative to the fifteen source-named inputs; retain unknown NaOH amount/form/concentration and final volume. Remove the unsupported second-adjustment implication from active notes and cases19/133; preserve original history and append an honest correction.",
      "identity_scope": "Case19 NBRC1308 occurrence only joins case133 NBRC1356. NBRC1020/824 remain excluded: KOH rather than NaOH, no NaCl/selenate/tungstate in the trace-stock table, and separate selenite/tungstate stock. The 200ml initial water instruction belongs to1020/824 and is not imported.",
      "processing_scope": "1308 stock dose1ml is in the autoclaved receiving mixture under N2/CO2(80/20).1356 stock dose10ml is filter-sterile in the N2-handled receiving medium. The complete medium pH9 is not the stock pH7. These contextual differences do not prove different nominal input substances or identical processed endpoints."
    },
